add('context','CTX1','Decision and boundary',dict(field='scope',value='Customers and support staff investigate outages, slow speed and billing errors. Automatic action is a service-ledger credit for a confirmed outage under H1. Speed, billing errors, large or unclear amounts go to a supervisor. Cash payouts, plan changes, network repair and historical inactive services are excluded. Start: authenticated complaint or provisional intake. End: evidence-backed explanation plus posted credit, no-credit finding, cancelled case, or an owned unresolved case with next update time.',question=''))
add('context','CTX2','Authoritative evidence',dict(field='records',value='Identity gateway supplies tenantId/customerId and scoped service choices. Account registry supplies active connection and version. Billing ledger supplies original recurring charge, cycle boundaries and already credited amount. Service telemetry supplies outage IDs, verified intervals, region and freshness. Published policy registry supplies signed effective version. Missing or contradictory evidence yields provisional human investigation; it does not prove no outage. Customer text may locate evidence but cannot override a record.',question=''))
add('context','CTX3','Delivery and success',dict(field='success',value='Reduce elapsed resolution hours without wrong-customer or duplicate credit. Business baseline unknown: collect two weeks before experiment. All control fixtures are synthetic specifications, not executed business tests. Adapter support, policy authority, queue staffing and privacy sign-off are launch blockers H1–H4,H6. All times are UTC instants and elapsed hours, independent of browser session.',question=''))
